{{> breadcrumbs}}

<h1 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text-100 mb-2">Setup</h1>
<p class="text-text-200 mb-6">Connect an AI assistant to Lorekeeper and start building worlds together.</p>

<!-- Tabs -->
<div class="border-b border-surface-300 mb-6">
  <nav class="flex gap-1" id="setup-tabs">
    <button data-tab="connect" class="tab-btn px-4 py-2.5 text-sm font-medium rounded-t-lg border border-b-0 border-surface-300 bg-surface-100 text-text-100 -mb-px">Connect</button>
    <button data-tab="skill" class="tab-btn px-4 py-2.5 text-sm font-medium rounded-t-lg text-text-300 hover:text-text-200 hover:bg-surface-200">Skill File</button>
    <button data-tab="tools" class="tab-btn px-4 py-2.5 text-sm font-medium rounded-t-lg text-text-300 hover:text-text-200 hover:bg-surface-200">Tools Reference</button>
  </nav>
</div>

<!-- Tab: Connect -->
<div id="tab-connect" class="tab-content space-y-6">
  <div class="bg-surface-100 rounded-lg border border-surface-300 p-6">
    <p class="text-text-200">The Model Context Protocol (MCP) lets AI assistants interact with Lorekeeper directly — creating worlds, characters, stories, and lore through conversation. Choose the connection method that matches your setup.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="bg-surface-100 rounded-lg border border-surface-300 p-6">
    <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-1">
      <span class="bg-ember-500 text-white text-xs font-bold px-2 py-0.5 rounded">Recommended</span>
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-text-100">Connect via URL</h2>
    </div>
    <p class="text-sm text-text-300 mb-5">Point your MCP client at the running Lorekeeper server. Requires <code class="bg-surface-200 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">npm run dev</code> to be running.</p>

    <div class="space-y-5">
      <div class="border-l-2 border-ember-400 pl-4">
        <h3 class="font-medium text-text-100 mb-2">Claude Desktop</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-text-300 mb-2">Edit <code class="bg-surface-200 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">claude_desktop_config.json</code>:</p>
        <pre class="bg-surface-50 text-green-400 rounded-lg p-3 overflow-x-auto text-sm"><code>{
  "mcpServers": {
    "lorekeeper": {
      "url": "http://localhost:3000/mcp"
    }
  }
}</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="border-l-2 border-ember-400 pl-4">
        <h3 class="font-medium text-text-100 mb-2">Claude Code</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-text-300 mb-2">Add to <code class="bg-surface-200 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">.claude/settings.json</code>:</p>
        <pre class="bg-surface-50 text-green-400 rounded-lg p-3 overflow-x-auto text-sm"><code>{
  "mcpServers": {
    "lorekeeper": {
      "url": "http://localhost:3000/mcp"
    }
  }
}</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="border-l-2 border-ember-400 pl-4">
        <h3 class="font-medium text-text-100 mb-2">Cursor / Cursor Agent</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-text-300 mb-2">Settings &rarr; MCP &rarr; Add Server &rarr; type <strong>URL</strong>:</p>
        <pre class="bg-surface-50 text-green-400 rounded-lg p-3 overflow-x-auto text-sm"><code>http://localhost:3000/mcp</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="bg-surface-100 rounded-lg border border-surface-300 p-6">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-text-100 mb-1">Connect via stdio</h2>
    <p class="text-sm text-text-300 mb-5">The MCP client spawns the server as a local process. No web server needed — communicates over stdin/stdout.</p>

    <div class="space-y-5">
      <div class="border-l-2 border-surface-400 pl-4">
        <h3 class="font-medium text-text-100 mb-2">Claude Desktop</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-text-300 mb-2">Edit <code class="bg-surface-200 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">claude_desktop_config.json</code>:</p>
        <pre class="bg-surface-50 text-green-400 rounded-lg p-3 overflow-x-auto text-sm"><code>{
  "mcpServers": {
    "lorekeeper": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["tsx", "{{projectPath}}/src/mcp-server.ts"],
      "env": {
        "DATABASE_URL": "file:{{projectPath}}/prisma/dev.db"
      }
    }
  }
}</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="border-l-2 border-surface-400 pl-4">
        <h3 class="font-medium text-text-100 mb-2">Claude Code</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-text-300 mb-2">Add to <code class="bg-surface-200 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">.claude/settings.json</code>:</p>
        <pre class="bg-surface-50 text-green-400 rounded-lg p-3 overflow-x-auto text-sm"><code>{
  "mcpServers": {
    "lorekeeper": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["tsx", "{{projectPath}}/src/mcp-server.ts"],
      "env": {
        "DATABASE_URL": "file:{{projectPath}}/prisma/dev.db"
      }
    }
  }
}</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="border-l-2 border-surface-400 pl-4">
        <h3 class="font-medium text-text-100 mb-2">Cursor / Cursor Agent</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-text-300 mb-2">Settings &rarr; MCP &rarr; Add Server &rarr; type <strong>Command</strong>:</p>
        <pre class="bg-surface-50 text-green-400 rounded-lg p-3 overflow-x-auto text-sm"><code>npx tsx {{projectPath}}/src/mcp-server.ts</code></pre>
        <p class="text-sm text-text-300 mt-2">Set env var: <code class="bg-surface-200 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">DATABASE_URL=file:{{projectPath}}/prisma/dev.db</code></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- Tab: Skill File -->
<div id="tab-skill" class="tab-content hidden space-y-6">
  <div class="bg-surface-100 rounded-lg border border-surface-300 p-6">
    <p class="text-text-200 mb-4">The skill file teaches your AI assistant how to be a world-building collaborator. It knows how to use all 22 Lorekeeper tools, follows a story generation workflow, and extracts lore artifacts automatically.</p>
    <p class="text-text-200">Install it once and the AI will guide you through creating characters, generating stories, and curating lore — no manual tool calls needed.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="bg-surface-100 rounded-lg border border-surface-300 p-6">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-text-100 mb-3">Installation</h2>
    <div class="space-y-5">
      <div class="border-l-2 border-ember-400 pl-4">
        <h3 class="font-medium text-text-100 mb-2">Claude Code</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-text-300 mb-2">Copy the skill file into your Claude Code skills directory:</p>
        <pre class="bg-surface-50 text-green-400 rounded-lg p-3 overflow-x-auto text-sm"><code>cp {{projectPath}}/skills/lorekeeper-advisor.md ~/.claude/skills/</code></pre>
        <p class="text-sm text-text-300 mt-2">Then use it with: <code class="bg-surface-200 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">/skill lorekeeper-advisor</code></p>
      </div>
      <div class="border-l-2 border-ember-400 pl-4">
        <h3 class="font-medium text-text-100 mb-2">Claude Desktop</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-text-300 mb-2">Add the skill file content as a project-level instruction. The file is at:</p>
        <pre class="bg-surface-50 text-green-400 rounded-lg p-3 overflow-x-auto text-sm"><code>{{projectPath}}/skills/lorekeeper-advisor.md</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="border-l-2 border-ember-400 pl-4">
        <h3 class="font-medium text-text-100 mb-2">Cursor / Cursor Agent</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-text-300 mb-2">Paste the skill file content into your project rules (<code class="bg-surface-200 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">.cursorrules</code>) or system prompt. The file is at:</p>
        <pre class="bg-surface-50 text-green-400 rounded-lg p-3 overflow-x-auto text-sm"><code>{{projectPath}}/skills/lorekeeper-advisor.md</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="bg-surface-100 rounded-lg border border-surface-300 p-6">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-text-100 mb-3">What the advisor does</h2>
    <div class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3">
      <div class="p-4 bg-surface-200 rounded-lg">
        <h3 class="font-medium text-text-100 mb-1">Builds worlds</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-text-200">Creates rich characters and evocative locations through conversation. Asks the right questions to draw out interesting details.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="p-4 bg-surface-200 rounded-lg">
        <h3 class="font-medium text-text-100 mb-1">Generates stories</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-text-200">Writes stories grounded in your world's existing characters, locations, and lore. Saves them with proper links and extracts new lore artifacts.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="p-4 bg-surface-200 rounded-lg">
        <h3 class="font-medium text-text-100 mb-1">Maintains consistency</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-text-200">Periodically checks for contradictions, suggests connections between characters and locations, and builds continuity across stories.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="bg-surface-100 rounded-lg border border-surface-300 p-6">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-text-100 mb-3">Example session</h2>
    <div class="space-y-3 text-sm">
      <div class="flex gap-3">
        <span class="text-text-300 font-medium shrink-0">You:</span>
        <span class="text-text-200">"I want to build a world set in a coastal town where magic is fading."</span>
      </div>
      <div class="flex gap-3">
        <span class="text-ember-400 font-medium shrink-0">AI:</span>
        <span class="text-text-200">Creates the world, asks about the town's history, who lives there, what the magic used to do...</span>
      </div>
      <div class="flex gap-3">
        <span class="text-text-300 font-medium shrink-0">You:</span>
        <span class="text-text-200">"Tell me a story about the lighthouse keeper discovering something in the tide pools."</span>
      </div>
      <div class="flex gap-3">
        <span class="text-ember-400 font-medium shrink-0">AI:</span>
        <span class="text-text-200">Writes the story using your characters and locations, saves it, extracts lore artifacts like "the tide pools glow faintly at new moon" and "Maren always hums while she works."</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- Tab: Tools Reference -->
<div id="tab-tools" class="tab-content hidden space-y-6">
  <div class="bg-surface-100 rounded-lg border border-surface-300 p-6">
    <p class="text-text-200">These are the 22 MCP tools available to any connected AI assistant. You don't need to call these manually if you're using the skill file — the advisor handles them. This reference is for custom integrations or debugging.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="bg-surface-100 rounded-lg border border-surface-300 p-6">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-text-100 mb-3">CRUD Tools</h2>
    <div class="grid gap-px bg-surface-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
      <div class="bg-surface-100 p-3 flex justify-between"><code class="text-ember-400 text-sm">list_worlds</code><span class="text-sm text-text-300">List all worlds</span></div>
      <div class="bg-surface-100 p-3 flex justify-between"><code class="text-ember-400 text-sm">get_world</code><span class="text-sm text-text-300">Get world details and stats</span></div>
      <div class="bg-surface-100 p-3 flex justify-between"><code class="text-ember-400 text-sm">create_world</code><span class="text-sm text-text-300">Create a new world</span></div>
      <div class="bg-surface-100 p-3 flex justify-between"><code class="text-ember-400 text-sm">update_world</code><span class="text-sm text-text-300">Update world name/description</span></div>
      <div class="bg-surface-100 p-3 flex justify-between"><code class="text-ember-400 text-sm">delete_world</code><span class="text-sm text-text-300">Delete a world and all contents</span></div>
      <div class="bg-surface-100 p-3 flex justify-between"><code class="text-ember-400 text-sm">list_characters</code><span class="text-sm text-text-300">List characters in a world</span></div>
      <div class="bg-surface-100 p-3 flex justify-between"><code class="text-ember-400 text-sm">get_character</code><span class="text-sm text-text-300">Get character with description</span></div>
      <div class="bg-surface-100 p-3 flex justify-between"><code class="text-ember-400 text-sm">create_character</code><span class="text-sm text-text-300">Create a character</span></div>
      <div class="bg-surface-100 p-3 flex justify-between"><code class="text-ember-400 text-sm">update_character</code><span class="text-sm text-text-300">Update character</span></div>
      <div class="bg-surface-100 p-3 flex justify-between"><code class="text-ember-400 text-sm">delete_character</code><span class="text-sm text-text-300">Delete a character</span></div>
      <div class="bg-surface-100 p-3 flex justify-between"><code class="text-ember-400 text-sm">list_locations</code><span class="text-sm text-text-300">List locations in a world</span></div>
      <div class="bg-surface-100 p-3 flex justify-between"><code class="text-ember-400 text-sm">get_location</code><span class="text-sm text-text-300">Get location with description</span></div>
      <div class="bg-surface-100 p-3 flex justify-between"><code class="text-ember-400 text-sm">create_location</code><span class="text-sm text-text-300">Create a location</span></div>
      <div class="bg-surface-100 p-3 flex justify-between"><code class="text-ember-400 text-sm">update_location</code><span class="text-sm text-text-300">Update location</span></div>
      <div class="bg-surface-100 p-3 flex justify-between"><code class="text-ember-400 text-sm">delete_location</code><span class="text-sm text-text-300">Delete a location</span></div>
      <div class="bg-surface-100 p-3 flex justify-between"><code class="text-ember-400 text-sm">list_stories</code><span class="text-sm text-text-300">List stories in a world</span></div>
      <div class="bg-surface-100 p-3 flex justify-between"><code class="text-ember-400 text-sm">get_story</code><span class="text-sm text-text-300">Get story with related data</span></div>
      <div class="bg-surface-100 p-3 flex justify-between"><code class="text-ember-400 text-sm">delete_story</code><span class="text-sm text-text-300">Delete a story</span></div>
      <div class="bg-surface-100 p-3 flex justify-between"><code class="text-ember-400 text-sm">list_lore</code><span class="text-sm text-text-300">List lore artifacts (filterable)</span></div>
      <div class="bg-surface-100 p-3 flex justify-between"><code class="text-ember-400 text-sm">update_lore_status</code><span class="text-sm text-text-300">Keep or discard lore</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="bg-surface-100 rounded-lg border border-surface-300 p-6">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-text-100 mb-3">Generation Tools</h2>
    <div class="grid gap-px bg-surface-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
      <div class="bg-surface-100 p-3 flex justify-between"><code class="text-ember-400 text-sm">get_world_context</code><span class="text-sm text-text-300">Full world context for AI generation</span></div>
      <div class="bg-surface-100 p-3 flex justify-between"><code class="text-ember-400 text-sm">save_story</code><span class="text-sm text-text-300">Save a story with character/location links</span></div>
      <div class="bg-surface-100 p-3 flex justify-between"><code class="text-ember-400 text-sm">save_lore_artifacts</code><span class="text-sm text-text-300">Save a batch of lore artifacts from a story</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="bg-surface-100 rounded-lg border border-surface-300 p-6">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-text-100 mb-3">Advisory Tools</h2>
    <div class="grid gap-px bg-surface-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
      <div class="bg-surface-100 p-3 flex justify-between"><code class="text-ember-400 text-sm">check_consistency</code><span class="text-sm text-text-300">World data for consistency review</span></div>
      <div class="bg-surface-100 p-3 flex justify-between"><code class="text-ember-400 text-sm">suggest_connections</code><span class="text-sm text-text-300">Character/location data for connection ideas</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<script>
document.querySelectorAll('.tab-btn').forEach(btn => {
  btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
    const tab = btn.dataset.tab;
    document.querySelectorAll('.tab-content').forEach(c => c.classList.add('hidden'));
    document.getElementById('tab-' + tab).classList.remove('hidden');
    document.querySelectorAll('.tab-btn').forEach(b => {
      b.className = 'tab-btn px-4 py-2.5 text-sm font-medium rounded-t-lg text-text-300 hover:text-text-200 hover:bg-surface-200';
    });
    btn.className = 'tab-btn px-4 py-2.5 text-sm font-medium rounded-t-lg border border-b-0 border-surface-300 bg-surface-100 text-text-100 -mb-px';
  });
});
</script>
